## Step 1 — Install ESP32 Board Support
**## download the arduino app at:https://www.arduino.cc/en/software
1. Open Arduino IDE
2. Go to **File → Preferences**
3. Find the field: **Additional boards manager URLs**
4. Paste this URL: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/espressif/arduino-esp32/gh-pages/package_esp32_index.json
5. Click **OK**
6. Go to **Tools → Board → Boards Manager**
7. Search: `esp32`
8. Find **esp32 by Espressif Systems**
9. Click **Install** — wait for download to complete
10. Go to **Tools → Board → ESP32 Arduino → AI Thinker ESP32-CAM**

---

## Step 2 — Install EloquentEsp32cam

1. Go to **Sketch → Include Library → Manage Libraries**
2. Search: `EloquentEsp32cam`
3. Find **EloquentEsp32cam by eloquentarduino**
4. Click **Install**

---

## Step 3 — Install WiFiManager

1. Go to **Sketch → Include Library → Manage Libraries**
2. Search: `WiFiManager`
3. Find **WiFiManager by tzapu**
4. Click **Install**

---

## Step 4 — Flash Settings

| Setting | Value |
|---|---|
| Board | AI Thinker ESP32-CAM |
| Partition Scheme | Huge APP (3MB No OTA) |
| CPU Frequency | 240MHz |
| Upload Speed | 115200 |
| Port | Your USB-to-UART adapter |

---

## Step 5 — First Boot WiFi Setup

1. Power on VisionBot
2. Connect your phone or laptop to: **SSID: `2DoFCVBOT`**
3. Password: `computervision`
4. A captive portal opens — enter your LAN credentials
5. VisionBot saves them and connects automatically on reboot

